<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">
  <Fragment>
    <!--
      Windows Defender Exclusion Custom Actions for MSI installer.
      Uses the same Directory+ExeCommand deferred pattern as the WebView2 bootstrapper.
      The MSI uses InstallScope="perMachine" so it already runs elevated via UAC.
    -->

    <!--
      REMOVED 2026-07-07 — install-time `AddDefenderExclusions`.

      The installer used to preemptively run `Add-MpPreference` with
      `-ExclusionPath` (INSTALLDIR + wildcard per-user \miners\ \monero\
      \zephyr\) AND `-ExclusionProcess` for xmrig.exe / lolMiner.exe /
      SRBMiner-MULTI.exe / rigel.exe / monero-wallet-rpc.exe /
      zephyr-wallet-rpc.exe. That has been deleted. Why:

        1. AV posture (the main reason). An installer that silently
           whitelists *miner processes* in Defender is a textbook
           coin-miner-dropper IOC. It is more likely to get the MSI
           flagged by Defender/SmartScreen behavioural detection than
           shipping the miner binaries ever was — and we no longer ship
           any miner binaries at all (they are download-on-demand since
           the 2026-07-06 de-bundle), so the installer had become the
           single largest remaining flag surface.
        2. Consent + correctness. Mining is opt-in as of 2026-07-06
           ([[mining-opt-in-gate]]): a fresh wallet runs zero mining code.
           Whitelisting miners at install fired for *every* user,
           including the majority who never enable mining. Weakening a
           user's AV without asking, for a feature they never turned on,
           is not something an install should do silently.

      The exclusions now happen at RUNTIME, at the moment the user opts in
      and can see what they are agreeing to — promoted from "fallback" to
      the mechanism:
        - `add_defender_exclusions`     (miners.rs)  — miners dir; surfaced
          by MinerSetupView's "Add Exclusions" button in the setup flow the
          MiningSetupWizard hands off to.
        - `xmr_add_defender_exclusion`  (xmr_rpc.rs) — monero dir, offered
          by the XMR sync surface when that sidecar is actually used.
        - `zph_add_defender_exclusion`  (zph_rpc.rs) — zephyr dir, ditto.

      `RemoveDefenderExclusions` below is deliberately KEPT on uninstall:
      it still cleans up exclusions added by an older MSI *and* any added
      at runtime by the commands above. Removing an exclusion is not a
      flag-worthy action, and leaving stale AV holes behind on uninstall
      would be worse.
    -->

    <!--
      Sprint 2 Phase 4 (install-time portion): defensive WinRing0 pre-clear.
      If a previous version of HWiNFO / MSI Afterburner / OpenRGB / Ryzen
      Master / etc. has registered WinRing0_1_2_0 on this machine, delete
      it now so PwndaWallet's launcher.cmd starts from a clean slate. The
      runtime portion is in xmrig-launcher.cmd (sc stop/delete on every
      mining start, inside the elevated Scheduled Task — no UAC).
    -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="ClearWinRing0Collision"
      Directory="INSTALLDIR"
      Execute="deferred"
      ExeCommand='cmd.exe /c "sc stop WinRing0_1_2_0 1&gt;nul 2&gt;&amp;1 &amp; sc delete WinRing0_1_2_0 1&gt;nul 2&gt;&amp;1 &amp; exit /b 0"'
      Return="ignore"
    />

    <!-- Remove Defender exclusions during uninstall. KEPT on purpose: cleans up
         exclusions added by an older MSI (which used to add them at install)
         AND any added at runtime by the opt-in commands. -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="RemoveDefenderExclusions"
      Directory="INSTALLDIR"
      Execute="deferred"
      ExeCommand='powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command "Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionPath &apos;[INSTALLDIR]&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionPath &apos;C:\Users\*\AppData\Roaming\com.pwnda.wallet\miners&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionPath &apos;C:\Users\*\AppData\Roaming\com.pwnda.wallet\monero&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionPath &apos;C:\Users\*\AppData\Roaming\com.pwnda.wallet\zephyr&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionProcess &apos;xmrig.exe&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionProcess &apos;lolMiner.exe&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionProcess &apos;SRBMiner-MULTI.exe&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionProcess &apos;monero-wallet-rpc.exe&apos;; Remove-MpPreference -ExclusionProcess &apos;zephyr-wallet-rpc.exe&apos;"'
      Return="ignore"
    />

    <!--
      Sprint 4 — Clean uninstall.
      The Sprint 1 Scheduled Task and WinRing0 driver registration both
      survive past app uninstall by default. These three custom actions
      remove them so a user uninstalling PwndaWallet ends up with a clean
      machine: no PwndaXmrig task in Task Scheduler, no orphan WinRing0
      service, no leftover xmrig.exe / WinRing0x64.sys / xmrig.log /
      task XML / launcher.cmd in their per-user APPDATA.

      IMPORTANT: We intentionally only remove the `miners` SUBDIRECTORY
      under `com.pwnda.wallet`, not the parent. The parent contains
      wallet vault data, settings, and Monero/Zephyr sidecar wallets —
      user data the user may want to keep across reinstalls.

      Condition: REMOVE~="ALL" AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE — fires on
      genuine user-initiated uninstall but not when the MSI is removing
      the old version as part of an in-place upgrade. Without that
      guard, upgrades would delete the task and force the user through
      the first-mining-start UAC prompt every upgrade.
    -->

    <!-- Remove the PwndaXmrig Scheduled Task -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="RemoveXmrigScheduledTask"
      Directory="INSTALLDIR"
      Execute="deferred"
      ExeCommand='cmd.exe /c "schtasks /delete /tn &quot;PwndaXmrig&quot; /f 1&gt;nul 2&gt;&amp;1 &amp; exit /b 0"'
      Return="ignore"
    />

    <!-- Stop and remove the WinRing0_1_2_0 kernel driver service -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="RemoveWinRing0Service"
      Directory="INSTALLDIR"
      Execute="deferred"
      ExeCommand='cmd.exe /c "sc stop WinRing0_1_2_0 1&gt;nul 2&gt;&amp;1 &amp; sc delete WinRing0_1_2_0 1&gt;nul 2&gt;&amp;1 &amp; exit /b 0"'
      Return="ignore"
    />

    <!--
      Remove the per-user runtime binary subdirectories across all user
      profiles on the machine (the MSI runs in machine context and
      cannot resolve the interactive user's APPDATA from a deferred
      CA, so we enumerate C:\Users\* explicitly).

      Cleaned subdirectories (each contains AV-flagged binaries that
      should not survive uninstall):
        - \miners\  — xmrig, lolMiner, SRBMiner + WinRing0x64.sys
        - \monero\  — monero-wallet-rpc.exe + scan database
        - \zephyr\  — zephyr-wallet-rpc.exe + scan database

      We touch ONLY those subdirectories — the parent
      com.pwnda.wallet directory is preserved (wallet vault, settings,
      xmr-wallets, zph-wallets, tauri-plugin-store).
    -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="RemoveRuntimeMinersDir"
      Directory="INSTALLDIR"
      Execute="deferred"
      ExeCommand='powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command "Get-ChildItem -Path C:\Users -Directory -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object { foreach ($sub in @(&apos;miners&apos;,&apos;monero&apos;,&apos;zephyr&apos;)) { $p = Join-Path $_.FullName (&apos;AppData\Roaming\com.pwnda.wallet\&apos; + $sub); if (Test-Path $p) { Remove-Item -Path $p -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue } } }"'
      Return="ignore"
    />

    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <!--
        NOTE: there is deliberately NO install-time Defender action here any
        more (removed 2026-07-07 — see the comment at the top of this file).
        Exclusions are added at runtime, on mining opt-in, with user consent.
      -->
      <!-- Pre-clear WinRing0 collision during install (defensive).
           Re-anchored to InstallFinalize now that AddDefenderExclusions,
           which it used to sequence After, no longer exists. -->
      <Custom Action="ClearWinRing0Collision" Before="InstallFinalize">
        <![CDATA[NOT REMOVE]]>
      </Custom>

      <!--
        Sprint 4 clean-uninstall sequence — fires on user-initiated
        uninstall only (NOT on upgrade-driven removal of the old MSI).
        Order: task → service → runtime files → defender exclusions.
      -->
      <Custom Action="RemoveXmrigScheduledTask" Before="RemoveDefenderExclusions">
        <![CDATA[REMOVE~="ALL" AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE]]>
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="RemoveWinRing0Service" After="RemoveXmrigScheduledTask">
        <![CDATA[REMOVE~="ALL" AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE]]>
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="RemoveRuntimeMinersDir" After="RemoveWinRing0Service">
        <![CDATA[REMOVE~="ALL" AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE]]>
      </Custom>

      <!-- Remove exclusions during uninstall -->
      <Custom Action="RemoveDefenderExclusions" Before="InstallFinalize">
        <![CDATA[REMOVE~="ALL"]]>
      </Custom>
    </InstallExecuteSequence>
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
